ser_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"referenced","commit_id":"436cb7221ffca29fd7764a022b8f7b35abd272bd","commit_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/commits/436cb7221ffca29fd7764a022b8f7b35abd272bd","created_at":"2024-03-22T14:34:27Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/2031644398","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/11173#issuecomment-2031644398","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/11173","id":2031644398,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCX5JB855GG7u","user":{"login":"AurelienJoy","id":143094889,"node_id":"U_kgDOCId0aQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/143094889?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AurelienJoy","html_url":"https://github.com/AurelienJoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AurelienJoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AurelienJoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AurelienJoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AurelienJoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AurelienJoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AurelienJoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AurelienJoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AurelienJoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AurelienJoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-04-02T10:31:51Z","updated_at":"2024-04-02T10:32:46Z","body":"Hello, \r\n\r\nfor information, this issue seems to also impact queries with `selectinload` and mysql dialect (at least). \r\n\r\nHere is a standalone script to reproduce the issue:\r\n\r\n## Broken requirements:\r\n```\r\npytest\r\nsqlalchemy==2.0.28\r\nmysqlclient==2.1.1\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Working requirements:\r\n```\r\npytest\r\nsqlalchemy==2.0.27\r\nmysqlclient==2.1.1\r\n```\r\n\r\n## The test\r\nThe following script expects a working mysql database and can be run as follows:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nDB_HOST=\"db-host\" \\\r\nDB_USER=\"db-user\" \\\r\nDB_PASSWORD=\"db-password\" \\\r\nDB_DATABASE=\"db-database\" \\\r\npytest test_sql_search.py\r\n```\r\n\r\n```python\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import Column, ForeignKey, Integer, String, create_engine\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import declarative_base, relationship, selectinload, sessionmaker\r\n\r\nBase = declarative_base()\r\n\r\n\r\nclass SubSubItem(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = \"sub_sub_items\"\r\n\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True, autoincrement=True)\r\n\r\n    sub_item_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(\"sub_items.id\"))\r\n    sub_item = relationship(\"SubItem\", back_populates=\"sub_sub_items\")\r\n    name = Column(String(255))\r\n\r\n\r\nclass SubItem(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = \"sub_items\"\r\n\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True, autoincrement=True)\r\n\r\n    item_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(\"items.id\"))\r\n    item = relationship(\"Item\", back_populates=\"sub_items\")\r\n\r\n    name = Column(String(255))\r\n\r\n    sub_sub_items = relationship(\r\n        \"SubSubItem\",\r\n        cascade=\"all, delete-orphan\",\r\n    )\r\n\r\n\r\nclass Item(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = \"items\"\r\n\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True, autoincrement=True)\r\n    sub_items = relationship(\"SubItem\", back_populates=\"item\")\r\n\r\n\r\ndef create_session():\r\n    DB_HOST = os.getenv(\"DB_HOST\")\r\n    DB_USER = os.getenv(\"DB_USER\")\r\n    DB_PASSWORD = os.getenv(\"DB_PASSWORD\")\r\n    DB_DATABASE = os.getenv(\"DB_DATABASE\")\r\n\r\n    assert DB_HOST is not None, \"database host must be set\"\r\n    assert DB_USER is not None, \"database user must be set\"\r\n    assert DB_PASSWORD is not None, \"database password must be set\"\r\n    assert DB_DATABASE is not None, \"database must be set\"\r\n\r\n    engine = create_engine(f\"mysql://{DB_USER}:{DB_PASSWORD}@{DB_HOST}/{DB_DATABASE}\")\r\n    Base.metadata.drop_all(bind=engine)\r\n    Base.metadata.create_all(bind=engine)\r\n    return sessionmaker(bind=engine)\r\n\r\n\r\ndef test_create_items():\r\n    SessionLocal = create_session()\r\n\r\n    with SessionLocal() as db:\r\n        # Creating 2 items, first one without sub_item, second one with a sub_item\r\n        item_without_subitem = Item()\r\n        db.add(item_without_subitem)\r\n        item_with_subitem = Item()\r\n        db.add(item_with_subitem)\r\n        db.commit()\r\n        item_with_subitem.sub_items = [SubItem(name=\"dummy\")]\r\n        db.commit()\r\n\r\n    with SessionLocal() as db:\r\n\r\n        def query(id: int):\r\n            base_query = (\r\n                db.query(Item)\r\n                .options(\r\n                    selectinload(Item.sub_items.and_(SubItem.name.is_not(None))),\r\n                    selectinload(\r\n                        Item.sub_items,\r\n                        SubItem.sub_sub_items.and_(SubSubItem.name.is_not(None)),\r\n                    ),\r\n                )\r\n                .filter(Item.id == id)\r\n            )\r\n\r\n            return base_query.one()\r\n\r\n        # Following queries work with sqla 2.0.27 but does not work anymore with 2.0.28\r\n        item_without_sub_item = query(1)\r\n        item_with_sub_item = query(2)\r\n\r\n        # Queries order is important as interverting queries order \r\n        # (querying first the item with sub item then item without one) does work though\r\n        # item_with_sub_item = query(2)\r\n        # item_without_sub_item = query(1)\r\n\r\n        assert True\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Stacktrace \r\n\r\n```python\r\nm = <re.Match object; span=(199, 227), match='__[POSTCOMPILE_primary_keys]'>\r\n\r\n    def process_expanding(m):\r\n        key = m.group(1)\r\n>       expr = replacement_expressions[key]\r\nE       sqlalchemy.exc.StatementError: (builtins.KeyError) 'primary_keys'\r\nE       [SQL: SELECT sub_sub_items.sub_item_id AS sub_sub_items_sub_item_id, sub_sub_items.id AS sub_sub_items_id, sub_sub_items.name AS sub_sub_items_name\r\nE       FROM sub_sub_items\r\nE       WHERE sub_sub_items.sub_item_id IN (__[POSTCOMPILE_primary_keys]) AND sub_sub_items.name IS NOT NULL]\r\nE       [parameters: [{'primary_keys': [1]}]]\r\n```\r\n\r\nI've also tested with SQLA v2.0.29 and it works again so the bugfix https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/commit/436cb7221ffca29fd7764a022b8f7b35abd272bd seems to fix this case also.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/2031644398/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"AurelienJoy","id":143094889,"node_id":"U_kgDOCId0aQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/143094889?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AurelienJoy","html_url":"https://github.com/AurelienJoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AurelienJoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AurelienJoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AurelienJoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AurelienJoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AurelienJoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AurelienJoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AurelienJoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AurelienJoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AurelienJoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/2031779687","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/11173#issuecomment-2031779687","i